        "            log_loss(y_test, rf_prob),\n",
        "        ],\n",
        "    }\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "prob_scores"
      ],
      "id": "8eca7034",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The calibration curve compares predicted probabilities with observed frequencies. The Brier score and log loss summarize probability quality numerically.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Calibrating a Random Forest\n",
        "\n",
        "If a model ranks observations well but has poor calibration, we can calibrate it using held-out calibration folds."
